,"status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Environment Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Transport Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-01","committee":"Housing Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-07","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Moved; to 12 October","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Finance Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-12","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-27","committee":"Council Constitution","time":"","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Moved","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Moved","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Joint Pensions Committee","time":"7.15 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Health Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 p.m.","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Wandsworth pension costs soar as redundancies double forecasts","lead":"Wandsworth's pension fund faced near-double the expected costs from early retirements and redundancies in the year to March, with strain costs \u2014 the immediate pension payments triggered by staff leaving \u2014 reaching \u00a32.2m against a budget of \u00a31.2m. The fund's auditors at Ernst & Young said the number of redundancy and early retirement cases was almost double the previous year. The audit of the pension fund's accounts remains incomplete, with auditors still resolving valuation differences on two investments and correcting disclosure errors, including the incorrect classification of sterling-denominated assets in the fund's currency risk reporting.","iso":"2026-09-16","paper_title":"Paper No 26-195 Pension Fund External Audit Results Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128834/128834.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Joint Pensions Committee","paper_title":"Paper No 26-197 Pension Fund Annual Report 2025-26 - Appendix A PFAR","paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128843/128843.pdf","headline":"Pension strain costs nearly doubled year-on-year, indicating significant staff early retirements or redundancies","detail":"Strain costs (pension payments due to early retirement or redundancy) reached \u00a32.2m vs \u00a31.2m budgeted, with the report stating that 'The number of strain costs received this year was almost double last year.' This represents a material increase in unplanned staffing costs.","category":"people","matters":"Increased strain costs reflect additional pension liabilities incurred through workforce restructuring; this signals the council has undertaken substantial staffing changes that may reflect financial pressures requiring deeper investigation against the council's budget and savings plans.","figures":"Strain costs \u00a32.2m actual vs \u00a31.2m budgeted (82% variance); number of strain cost cases nearly double prior year","quote":"Employers strain costs. Strain costs specific to the individuals being made redundant/retiring early. The number of strain costs received this year was almost double last year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Joint Pensions Committee","paper_title":"Paper No 26-195 Pension Fund External Audit Results Report - Appendix A ARR","paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128835/128835.pdf","headline":"Audit opinion remains provisional pending resolution of multiple valuation and disclosure issues","detail":"Ernst & Young cannot issue a final opinion until completion of outstanding procedures: resolution of valuation differences on two investments (Level 2 Schroders \u00a33m and Level 3 unspecified), receipt of revised IAS 26 actuarial disclosures, completion of investment profit/loss work, and resolution of Currency Risk disclosure amendments. The report explicitly states work is 'subject to final review' on multiple material areas.","category":"audit","matters":"An unqualified audit opinion is the baseline expectation for fund administration; the number and nature of outstanding items indicate material issues remain unresolved as of the meeting date","figures":"7 categories of work remain outstanding; 5 require joint EY and management action","quote":"Subject to completion of the remaining outstanding procedures outlined in this report, including executive review, we expect to issue an unqualified opinion. Please refer to Appendix B for Outstanding matters.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Joint Pensions Committee","paper_title":"Paper No 26-195 Pension Fund External Audit Results Report - Appendix A ARR","paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128835/128835.pdf","headline":"Material prior-year disclosure error in Currency Risk note requires restatement of comparatives","detail":"The audit identified that Note 26 (Nature and Extent of Risks Arising from Financial Instruments) incorrectly included UK sterling denominated investments in the Currency Risk disclosure. Investments in sterling by definition carry no currency risk. This material error requires amendment of the current year and prior year comparative figures, indicating that financial statement review controls were inadequate in prior years.","category":"audit","matters":"Prior-year restatements reduce confidence in the reliability of the council's financial reporting controls; repeated disclosure errors indicate systemic issues in how the finance team prepares and reviews statements","figures":"Material issue requiring prior year adjustment","quote":"Our work on Note 26 Nature and Extent of Risks Arising from Financial Instruments is in progress, and has identified a material issue whereby the Currency Risk disclosure has included investments that are UK sterling denominated, and therefore do not have currency risk. This will also amend the prior year comparatives as a prior year adjustment.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Joint Pensions Committee","paper_title":"Paper No 26-195 Pension Fund External Audit Results Report - Appendix A ARR","paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128835/128835.pdf","headline":"Data version control failure caused incorrect cashflow data to be submitted to the fund actuary","detail":"The pension fund submitted an older version of cashflow data to the actuary due to a file-saving issue on the server, resulting in the wrong version being used prior to completion of review checks. While the impact was limited to the IAS 26 actuarial disclosures, this indicates that controls over data management and third-party submissions lack adequate review and approval procedures.","category":"governance","matters":"Data quality failures in pension fund administration suggest control weaknesses in the council's finance function; poor controls over actuarial data could lead to understated or overstated pension liabilities","figures":"One incorrect data submission; classified as Low control deficiency","quote":"An incorrect version of the Fund cashflow data was submitted to the actuary due to a file-saving issue on the server. The impact was limited to the IAS 26 report, which forms the basis of the actuarial disclosures within the financial statements.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-16","committee":"Joint Pensions Committee","paper_title":"Paper No 26-195 Pension Fund External Audit Results Report 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128834/128834.pdf","headline":"Audit complexity increased due to new team, regulatory requirements, and issues discovered during fieldwork","detail":"The new EY audit team for 2025/26 encountered more outstanding work than in recent years, partly attributable to increased audit requirements and partly to issues discovered during testing. The 2025/26 audit includes additional scope for the triennial valuation review, which is expected to lead to higher variation fees than the 2024/25 variation fee of \u00a38,502.","category":"audit","matters":"Higher audit complexity and variation fees may indicate increased risk or control issues in pension fund accounting; audit team changes can affect consistency and depth of findings.","figures":"2024/25 variation fee \u00a38,502; 2025/26 expected to be higher due to triennial valuation review","quote":"There is slightly more work outstanding at this point than in recent years. This is partly due to increased audit requirements requiring more work to the same deadline, and partly due to the issues discovered during the audit work.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-16"},"name":"Wandsworth","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-22","since_iso":"2026-08-23","distress":false,"headline":"Pension strain costs nearly doubled year-on-year, indicating significant staff early retirements or redundancies","lead":"Increased strain costs reflect additional pension liabilities incurred through workforce restructuring; this signals the council has undertaken substantial staffing changes that may reflect financial pressures requiring deeper investigation against the\u2026","also":["6 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Children's Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-22","n_findings":7,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Paper No 26-197 Pension Fund Annual Report 2025-26 - Appendix A PFAR","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.wandsworth.gov.uk/documents/s128843/128843.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":61,"news_drafts_total":1}}